<title>PHILIPPINES: Cebu Property sets 17 centavo cash div.</title>
<headline>Cebu Property sets 17 centavo cash div.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cebu Property Ventures &amp; Development Corp said on Wednesday its board had approved a 17 centavo cash dividend.</p>
<p>A 10 centavo cash regular dividend is due to shareholders as of June 25 and payable on July 25 this year.</p>
<p>The board also approved a special cash dividend of seven centavo per share to shareholders as of June 25.</p>
<p>The special cash dividend will be taken out of its first quarter income and is still subject to the approval of the Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>Cebu Property is a subsidiary of conglomerate Ayala Corp.</p>
<p>-- Manila Newsroom (63 2) 841-8938 Fax 817-6267</p>
